</div>

	<p>Open trailers, on the other hand, offer a more cost-effective option for bike transportation. Although they provide less protection compared to enclosed carriers, they still offer some advantages:</p>

	<ul>
		<li><strong>Cost-Effective:</strong> Open trailers are generally cheaper than enclosed carriers, making them an attractive choice for budget-conscious customers.</li>
		<li><strong>Slightly Better Weather Exposure:</strong> With limited protection from the elements, open trailers can expose your bike to some level of rain, dust, and wind, but the exposure is minimized compared to enclosed carriers.</li>
		<li><strong>Greater Visibility:</strong> Transporting your bike on an open trailer makes it visible, allowing you to keep an eye on it and ensure its safety during the journey.</li>
	</ul>

